{"name":"Blood Rush","hex":"#aa2222","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vital liquid flowing in the bodies of many types of animals that usually conveys nutrients and oxygen. In vertebrates, it is colored red by hemoglobin, is conveyed by arteries and veins, is pumped by the heart and is usually generated in bone marrow.","A family relationship due to birth, such as that between siblings; contrasted with relationships due to marriage or adoption. See blood relative, blood relation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause something to be covered with blood; to bloody.","To let blood (from); to bleed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blood"},{"term":"rush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sudden forward motion.","A surge, a sudden increase."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hurry; to perform a task with great haste, often not properly or without thinking carefully.","To flow or move forward rapidly or noisily."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blood Rush","blocks":[{"text":"\"Blood Rush\" is the eighth episode of the third season, and 52nd episode overall from the Fox series Gotham. The episode was written by Tze Chun and directed by Rob Bailey. It was first broadcast on November 7, 2016. In the episode, Barnes loses control of the effects of Alice Tetch's blood and begins to use his powers to target a killer, no matter the cost of those who stand in his way. Gordon is reinstated as detective and investigates along with Bullock the killer, who uses plastic surgery to fake identities. Meanwhile, Cobblepot tries to stop Isabella from continuing to see Nygma."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_Rush","wikidata":"Q27877383"},{"title":"Blood","blocks":[{"text":"Blood is a specialized form of connective tissue and body fluid in the circulatory system of humans and other vertebrates that delivers necessary substances such as nutrients and oxygen to the cells of the body, and transports metabolic waste products away from those same cells."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg/330px-Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood","wikidata":"Q7873"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/1GZX_Haemoglobin.png/500px-1GZX_Haemoglobin.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/1GZX_Haemoglobin.png/1280px-1GZX_Haemoglobin.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/1GZX_Haemoglobin.png/500px-1GZX_Haemoglobin.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hemoglobin, a globular proteingreen = haem (or heme) groupsred & blue = protein subunits","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1GZX_Haemoglobin.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Krew_Frakcjonowana.jpg/120px-Krew_Frakcjonowana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Krew_Frakcjonowana.jpg/250px-Krew_Frakcjonowana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Krew_Frakcjonowana.jpg/120px-Krew_Frakcjonowana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKrew_Frakcjonowana.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Blutkreislauf.png/120px-Blutkreislauf.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co